---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import Share from '../components/Share.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="About" description="About Dr. Binu Alexander, creator of Baxter, the Agentic BA.">
  <div class="border-b border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">About</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-8 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
      <img
        src={`${base}binu-alexander.png`}
        alt="Dr. Binu Alexander"
        class="h-20 w-20 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover"
      />
      <div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-2">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Dr. Binu Alexander</h2>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/drbinualexander/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-500 hover:text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-400 dark:hover:text-white"
          >
            <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433c-1.144 0-2.063-.926-2.063-2.065 0-1.138.92-2.063 2.063-2.063 1.14 0 2.064.925 2.064 2.063 0 1.139-.925 2.065-2.064 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/></svg>
            LinkedIn
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Business Analyst, ASC · India</p>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
          <p>
            I am a Business Analyst and Technology Consultant working at the intersection of Business Analysis, Software Engineering, Healthcare Information Technology and Digital Transformation, and my engagements typically involve requirements definition, stakeholder coordination, process design, risk assessment and solution validation, conducted from a base in India for clients across a range of regions and industries.
          </p>
          <p>
            My professional foundation began in clinical medicine, a discipline that shaped my approach to diagnostic reasoning, structured observation, evidence gathering and problem framing, before I moved into product leadership and the Information Technology industry, holding positions spanning product strategy, delivery oversight, cross-functional coordination and organizational change.
          </p>
          <p>
            My core strength lies in bringing engineering discipline to Business Analysis practice, and over time I grew concerned that Business Analysts lacked working conditions available to developers, among them version control, plain-text documentation, peer review and configuration management, which led me to create the Agentic Business Analysis Framework.
          </p>
          <p>
            In my engagements, my responsibilities have centered on requirements elicitation, solution review, stakeholder alignment, acceptance criteria definition and release governance across Healthcare Information Technology, Workplace Automation, NLP and Content Localization initiatives, and I have contributed to frameworks that verify requirements against the underlying codebase rather than against assumption alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            My technical toolkit includes Claris FileMaker Pro, JavaScript, SuiteScript and Python, which I apply to scripting, automation, integration design and prototyping, and this familiarity with implementation allows me to review and at times contribute to code directly, rather than relying solely on secondhand technical translation.
          </p>
          <p>
            I am known for parallel trench learning, an approach in which I pursue depth across several domains at once and draw connections between requirements engineering, clinical reasoning, software architecture, organizational behavior and systems thinking, and this disposition carries directly into my primary interest in the Agentic Business Analysis Framework, Harness Engineering, agent orchestration, workflow automation and code-grounded requirements practice.
          </p>
          <p>
            For engagements or conversations along these lines, I can be reached by email at <a href="mailto:binu@thedatadrivenlife.com" class="font-semibold text-primary-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary-700 dark:text-primary-400">binu@thedatadrivenlife.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Share />
  <CTA />
</Base>
